{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-214096","model_call":34,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"couch lock\" munchies cannabis)"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"couch lock\" munchies cannabis)"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_1620706128#17_3488418136","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q640","rank":1,"snippet":"Diablo 3 – Pineapple Express 4 – Tahoe OG Kush 5 – Candyland Final Thoughts on Marijuana & Appetite Disorders Published on: 25 Jul, 2018 \" , \"segment\": \"It contains 20-25% THC, and with practically zero CBD (as little as 0.07%), it is a very potent strain. When you use Tahoe OG Kush, you could feel relaxed within minutes if the cannabis strain works its magic. Users report feeling warm and cozy. Rather than experiencing <cover>couch-lock, you may feel an uplifting energy boost, which may help you get some work done. Most importantly, you become ready to raid the fridge, the cabinets, and your neighbor’s kitchen as the munchies hit hard. It is common for users of this cannabis </cover>strain to consume so many snacks that they ultimately fall into a food coma. If you have an appetite disorder, this sounds like a recipe for success. Tahoe OG Kush has a lovely pine fresh scent with an added sweetness that is immediately apparent. It tastes almost as sweet as it smells, and your taste buds will rejoice at the delicious lemon taste. This is arguably what stimulates appetite the most!\" , \"start_char\""},"time":246},"model_calls":34,"document_judgments":20,"relevance_3":9,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
