{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-214096","model_call":47,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ cannabis effects drowsiness hunger motivation)"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ cannabis effects drowsiness hunger motivation)"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_251322740#16_609574532","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q649","rank":1,"snippet":"Resources: Doctors Near You Dispensaries Near You Are You A Doctor? Helpful Resources \" , \"segment\": \"What counts as a side effect of marijuana is an effect you don’t want. But everyone wants different things from <cover>cannabis medicine, so your side effects will differ from another patient’s. For example, look at these effects of marijuana commonly cited as side effects that can help you as a cancer patient: Hunger/increased appetite: The extra hunger resulting from weed use can inconvenience some users. But, if your cancer or treatment reduces your appetite, marijuana can give you the motivation to eat a normal diet. Insomnia/energy boost: Like any other stimulant, sativa strains of marijuana can keep the user awake, especially if they take it too close to bedtime. As long as you make sure to medicate at a time that doesn’t conflict with bedtime, you can feel energized rather than restless. Drowsiness/</cover>sleep aid:\" , \"start_char\": 7845.000000 , \"title\": \"Medical Marijuana for Lung Cancer - Marijuana Doctors\" , \"url\": \"https://www.marijuanadoctors.com/conditions/lung-cancer/\" }"},"time":34},"model_calls":47,"document_judgments":29,"relevance_3":12,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
